cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "discoal Studio: reproducible discoal selective-sweep datasets on your own computer"
message: "If you use this software or data made with it, please cite it and discoal (Kern & Schrider 2016)."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Joarder
    given-names: Tanvir Anjum
    affiliation: Florida Atlantic University
    email: tjoarder2026@fau.edu
version: 0.2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/tanviranjumjoarder/discoal-studio"
url: "https://github.com/tanviranjumjoarder/discoal-studio"
date-released: "2026-10-20"
abstract: >-
  discoal Studio is a desktop application that designs, runs and checks
  selective-sweep simulation datasets with the coalescent simulator discoal.
  Users describe a dataset in physical units (or in plain English); the app
  compiles one reproducible discoal command per file, covering every discoal
  option, runs them in parallel on a laptop or exports them for SLURM, and
  provides quality-check statistics and machine-learning arrays.
keywords:
  - population genetics
  - selective sweeps
  - coalescent simulation
  - discoal
  - machine learning
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Discoal: flexible coalescent simulations with selection"
    authors:
      - family-names: Kern
        given-names: Andrew D.
      - family-names: Schrider
        given-names: Daniel R.
    journal: Bioinformatics
    volume: 32
    issue: 24
    start: 3839
    end: 3841
    year: 2016
    doi: 10.1093/bioinformatics/btw556
